<title>GREECE: TABLE OF GREEK MUTUAL FUND FLOWS, ASSETS.</title>
<headline>TABLE OF GREEK MUTUAL FUND FLOWS, ASSETS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ionian Bank reported the</p>
<p>following daily and year-to-date changes in the volume of Greek</p>
<p>mutual fund outstanding shares, net assets and net share prices,</p>
<p>as well as total net asset sizes as of May 30.</p>
<p>				    May 30/May 29   May 30/Dec 31, 96</p>
<p>						 (%)		  (%)</p>
<p>NET SHARE PRICES*</p>
<p>  Total market			   -0.07		 6.79</p>
<p>  Fixed income &amp;money market funds  0.02		 5.05</p>
<p>  International funds		  -0.41		 9.37</p>
<p>  Growth Funds			   -1.76		56.13</p>
<p>* Prices include distributed dividends</p>
<p>VOLUME OF SHARES</p>
<p>  Total market			   -1.14		30.08</p>
<p>  Fixed income &amp;money market funds -1.21		30.57</p>
<p>  International funds		   0.21		10.73</p>
<p>  Growth funds			    0.05		27.83</p>
<p>NET ASSETS</p>
<p>  Total market			   -1.20		37.24</p>
<p>  Fixed income &amp;money market funds -1.20		35.67</p>
<p>  International funds		  -0.23		18.63</p>
<p>  Growth funds			   -1.73		95.21</p>
<p>All calculations are based on a performance index of mutual</p>
<p>funds whose base was set to be equal to 100 on December 31,</p>
<p>1991.</p>
<p>NET ASSET SIZES (in drachmas)</p>
<p>  Total market				  5,219,478,042,613</p>
<p>  Fixed income funds			  1,921,439,615,456</p>
<p>  Money market funds			  2,965,300,284,819</p>
<p>  International funds			    93,255,512,178</p>
<p>  Growth funds				    239,482,530,159</p>
<p>--Angelos Kiosklis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
